hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15965","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Muhammad ibn Safwan: that he hunted two rabbits but found no iron to slaughter them with, so he slaughtered them with a flint. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who commanded him to eat them."
"15966","Yazid narrated to us, he said, Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, informed us, from Amir, from Muhammad ibn Safwan: that he passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two rabbits hanging, then he mentioned its meaning."
